15989.sol:
In damping harmonic oscillator, amplitude $\begin{aligned}& A=A_0 e^{-b t} \\
& \therefore A_1=A_0 e^{-b \times2} \Rightarrow \frac{A_1}{A_0}= e^{-2 b}
\end{aligned}$ And $\begin{aligned}& A_2=A_0 e^{-b \times4} \Rightarrow \frac{A_2}{A_0}= e^{-4 b}=\left( e^{-2 b}\right)^2=\left(\frac{A_1}{A_0}\right)^2 \\
& \text{ or, } \frac{A_2}{A_0}=\left(\frac{A_1}{A_0}\right)^2=\frac{A_1^2}{A_0^2} \text{ or, } \frac{A_2}{A_1^2}=\frac{1}{A_0} \therefore A_1=\sqrt{A_0 A_2}
\end{aligned}$

